FH6 runtime: live code buffers, chained growth, batched SMC erases

Applies on top of 0001-0003 and completes the series; the four patches
together reproduce bin/libarm64ecfex.dll in this repo.

- Count any live code buffer as JIT, not only the current chain, so a
  thread that migrated to a newer chain keeps working in an older one.
- Track live buffer ranges in a lockless registry that signal context can
  query.
- Continue the code buffer chain when growing instead of starting a new
  one; the replaced buffer used to be freed while exit links still
  pointed into its code.
- Queue SMC erases and erase runs of them under one write lock, with a
  reader gap between batches. The map lock favours writers, so one
  acquisition per event parked every reader.
- Carries the optional experiment flags documented in README:
  FEX_FH6_FASTUD, FEX_FH6_SPINSAMPLE, FEX_POOL_CLONE, FH6Stats counters.

